From 167e03d0e63d42a521dcab1513cdd67dce97357c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@users.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:26:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VPVulkan + Metal: exclusive per-encoder GPU time (gpu.excl,
 vertex/fragment split, attachment traffic), opt-in tracked command-buffer
 ordering (VP_CB_ORDER=2), opt-in multiview through Metal vertex amplification
 (VPVK_AMPLIFY=1) and native half vertex fetch (VPVK_FETCH_NATIVE=1)

- metal2: render encoders sample vertex start/end and fragment start/end; every
  completed command buffer is placed on one GPU timeline and each encoder gets
  its exclusive time (how far it moved the latest end), summed per command-buffer
  type and logged every VP_EXCL_SECONDS (5) s as gpu.excl lines with format, size,
  samples, draws, load/store actions + tile verdicts and their MB, vtx/frag spans
  (VP_EXCL_TIMING=0 turns it off).
- metal2: VP_CB_ORDER=2 joins only the encoders whose accesses (buffers by host
  address range, textures by identity) overlap a write of / are writes to what a
  command buffer still in flight uses, before the vertex or only the fragment stage;
  the join fence stays in the frontier. Default stays 1 (build 24 behaviour).
- shader/vulkan/metal2: VPVK_AMPLIFY=1 translates two-view multiview vertex shaders
  with [[amplification_id]] (layer/viewport index 0 + view mappings, no instance
  multiplication; ClipDistance/Layer writers keep instancing) and fragment ViewIndex
  through a flat varying; the backend sets maxVertexAmplificationCount and the
  encoder's amplification count per draw.
- spirv: VPVK_FETCH_NATIVE=1 converts half vertex attributes with one half2 conversion.
- Translator modes are part of the recipe store's translator id (kTranslatorVersion |
  modes << 16): a mode change retranslates the stored recipes; all off = id 4 as before.
